          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"flex-lab-test\">FLEX lab test</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A simulated two-PC lab (no hardware): <strong>PC A</strong> has a <code>bench</code> (gate \u2192 x), <strong>PC B</strong> a\n<code>spectrometer</code>, and one runner controls both. Things to try, top to bottom:</span>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Direct access</strong> \u2013 move the slider, <code>bench.x</code> follows; read the spectrometer.</li>\n<li><strong>Run <code>gate_sweep</code></strong> \u2192 <code>done</code>, with a plot.</li>\n<li><strong>Run <code>two_pcs</code></strong> \u2192 <code>done</code>, one script driving both PCs.</li>\n<li><strong>Run <code>long_run</code>, press Abort</strong> \u2192 <code>aborted</code>, and the log shows <code>cleaned up</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Run <code>failing</code></strong> \u2192 <code>failed</code>, with the error and traceback.</li>\n<li><strong>Press Run while another run is going</strong> \u2192 refused as busy.</li>\n<li><strong>Start <code>long_run</code>, close this window, double-click the launcher again</strong> \u2192 the run is still going.</li>\n</ol></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
